    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Jacob Wilson** and **Drake Baldwin** anchoring the offensive core. **Jacob Wilson** commands our highest confidence with a 71.63 score, benefiting significantly from a +10% park factor and an advantageous matchup against a left-handed arm, while **Drake Baldwin** holds the #1 spot in the order against a vulnerable Mikolas, providing the highest ceiling for runs scored. **Jackson Merrill** also presents a high-upside play at 69.24; his +13% dynamic platoon edge against Mahle is the primary driver, positioning him as a critical component in our quest to close the gap in the 5x5 standings.\n\nStrategic decisions today heavily weigh our need for stolen bases, a scarce commodity in our current build. **Nasim Nunez** (60.14) gets the start over **Denzer Guzman** (44.36) primarily due to this efficiency gap; **Denzer Guzman** was the closest to cracking the lineup, but his projected lower output against Gasser made him the logical sit. Meanwhile, we are managing significant headwinds with **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo**; both face a formidable pitcher in Sanchez, whose 2.84 xERA and elite ability to suppress steals significantly deflate their scores, dropping both into the low-50s despite their favorable batting positions.\n\nWe must remain vigilant regarding the risks inherent in today's matchups. **Gunnar Henderson** and **Coby Mayo** are specifically flagged for a combination of high-skill pitching and an elite catcher, which significantly hinders our potential to accrue stolen bases in those spots. **Sam Antonacci** is also a precarious start at 45.19, as he faces Rasmussen\u2014a tough arm in a pitcher-friendly environment. We are proceeding with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (64.59) as a reliable anchor, but the overall benching of **Miguel Vargas** below our 40-point floor highlights our commitment to preserving game caps and avoiding low-efficiency plate appearances in this competitive stretch.",
